From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slothfulchat <patches@slothfulchat.invalid>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 13:49:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 82/83] web-app: fix recorder gesture precedence, AudioContext
 leak, phone margins
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three follow-up fixes to the voice recorder, found reviewing the epic
after it landed.

1. Gesture: a diagonal up-AND-left "throw it away" flick locked the
   recording hands-free instead of cancelling it. The live pointermove
   handler locked the instant dy crossed LOCK_DY and set active=false,
   so the pointerup path — which runs classifyGesture, and classifyGesture
   checks cancel *before* lock — never ran. The unit-tested cancel-wins
   precedence was unreachable in the real gesture. Fix: the live handler
   now delegates to classifyGesture and live-locks only when it returns
   'lock', so cancel-over-lock holds on the move path too (covered by the
   existing "cancel wins over lock on a diagonal" case).

2. AudioContext leak: start() opens an AudioContext up front, before
   getUserMedia. On a gUM rejection (permission denied, or the stale-device
   fallback's retry also failing) the caller's error path does not call
   stop(), and stop() wouldn't close the context anyway — its teardown is
   gated on a microphone/processor that never got wired. Repeated failed
   attempts leaked contexts until the browser's concurrent-AudioContext cap
   (~6 in Chrome) started throwing. Fix: start() closes and nulls its own
   context on the reject path.

3. Phone-layout margins: the max-width:500px overrides for .cancel /
   .stopRecording are written outside .audioRecorder, while the base block
   nests them under it. So .cancel/.stopRecording (0,1,0) lose to
   .audioRecorder .cancel (0,2,0) for margin-inline-start, and the doubled
   .stopRecording.stopRecording (0,2,0) still loses to
   .audioRecorder .stopRecording.stopRecording (0,3,0) for margin-inline-end
   — the narrow-viewport margins silently didn't apply either way. Fix:
   prefix all three with .audioRecorder so specificity ties and later
   source order wins.
---
 .../src/components/AudioRecorder/AudioRecorder.tsx  |  6 +++++-
 .../src/components/AudioRecorder/MicRecorder.ts     | 10 ++++++++++
 .../src/components/AudioRecorder/styles.module.scss | 13 ++++++++-----
 3 files changed, 23 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/packages/frontend/src/components/AudioRecorder/AudioRecorder.tsx b/packages/frontend/src/components/AudioRecorder/AudioRecorder.tsx
index dc14d0a..9cfde87 100644
--- a/packages/frontend/src/components/AudioRecorder/AudioRecorder.tsx
+++ b/packages/frontend/src/components/AudioRecorder/AudioRecorder.tsx
@@ -516,7 +516,11 @@ export const AudioRecorder = ({
       const dy = ev.clientY - startY
       setSlideDx(Math.min(dx, 0))
       setCancelArmed(dx <= CANCEL_DX)
-      if (dy <= LOCK_DY) {
+      // Reuse the release path's precedence: classifyGesture checks cancel
+      // before lock, so a diagonal up-AND-left flick stays a cancel (finalized
+      // on `up`) instead of latching a lock the user was trying to throw away.
+      // Live-lock only when the gesture classifies as a pure lock.
+      if (classifyGesture(dx, dy, Date.now() - startT) === 'lock') {
         // Lock live: hands-free. Stop tracking and drop to the tap-to-stop row.
         active = false
         cleanup()
diff --git a/packages/frontend/src/components/AudioRecorder/MicRecorder.ts b/packages/frontend/src/components/AudioRecorder/MicRecorder.ts
index 9ba7f21..f1e2500 100644
--- a/packages/frontend/src/components/AudioRecorder/MicRecorder.ts
+++ b/packages/frontend/src/components/AudioRecorder/MicRecorder.ts
@@ -192,6 +192,16 @@ class MicRecorder {
           resolve(stream)
         })
         .catch(err => {
+          // getUserMedia (incl. the stale-device fallback) failed: close the
+          // AudioContext start() opened up-front. The caller's error path does
+          // not call stop(), and stop() wouldn't close it anyway (its cleanup
+          // is gated on a microphone/processor that never got wired), so
+          // repeated denials would otherwise leak contexts until the browser's
+          // concurrent-AudioContext cap throws.
+          if (this.context && this.context.state !== 'closed') {
+            this.context.close()
+          }
+          this.context = null
           reject(err)
         })
     })
diff --git a/packages/frontend/src/components/AudioRecorder/styles.module.scss b/packages/frontend/src/components/AudioRecorder/styles.module.scss
index 576489f..0ae60f3 100644
--- a/packages/frontend/src/components/AudioRecorder/styles.module.scss
+++ b/packages/frontend/src/components/AudioRecorder/styles.module.scss
@@ -374,13 +374,16 @@
   .previewControls {
     flex-basis: 100%;
   }
-  .cancel,
-  .stopRecording {
+  // Prefixed with `.audioRecorder` to match the base block, whose SCSS nesting
+  // compiles these to `.audioRecorder .cancel` / `.audioRecorder .stopRecording`
+  // (and `.audioRecorder .stopRecording.stopRecording`). Same specificity +
+  // later source order → these win. Without the prefix the base out-ranked them
+  // and the desktop margins leaked onto the phone layout.
+  .audioRecorder .cancel,
+  .audioRecorder .stopRecording {
     margin-inline-start: 6px;
   }
-  // Doubled class to out-rank the base block's nested `&.stopRecording`
-  // (margin-inline-end: 40px) at equal position-independent specificity.
-  .stopRecording.stopRecording {
+  .audioRecorder .stopRecording.stopRecording {
     margin-inline-end: 6px;
   }
   // Cancel/OK wrap together as a right-aligned pair instead of OK being
